      "extract": "DUALITY AND TILTING FOR COMMUTATIVE DG RINGS AMNON YEKUTIELI Abstract. We consider commutative DG rings (better known as nonpositive strongly commutative associative unital DG algebras). For such a DG ring A we de- ﬁne the notions of perfect, tilting, dualizing, Cohen-Macaulay and rigid DG A-modules. Geometrically perfect DG modules are deﬁned by a local condition on Spec ¯A, where ¯A is the commutative ring H0(A).",
